#: src/modules.md:1
msgid "Modules"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:3
msgid ""
"A `justfile` can declare modules using `mod` statements<sup>1.19.0</sup>."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:5
msgid "`mod` statements were stabilized in `just`<sup>1.31.0</sup>."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:7
msgid "If you have the following `justfile`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:16
msgid "And the following text in `bar.just`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:23
msgid ""
"`bar.just` will be included in `justfile` as a submodule. Recipes, aliases, "
"and variables defined in one submodule cannot be used in another, and each "
"module uses its own settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:27
msgid "Recipes in submodules can be invoked as subcommands:"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:34
msgid "Or with path syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:41
msgid ""
"If a module is named `foo`, `just` will search for the module file in `foo."
"just`, `foo/mod.just`, `foo/justfile`, and `foo/.justfile`. In the latter "
"two cases, the module file may have any capitalization."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:45
msgid "Module statements may be of the form:"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:51
msgid ""
"Which loads the module’s source file from `PATH`, instead of from the usual "
"locations. A leading `~/` in `PATH` is replaced with the current user’s home "
"directory. `PATH` may point to the module source file itself, or to a "
"directory containing the module source file with the name `mod.just`, "
"`justfile`, or `.justfile`. In the latter two cases, the module file may "
"have any capitalization."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:58
msgid ""
"Environment files are loaded for each module, respecting that module’s "
"related settings. Environment variables from parent modules are visible in "
"child modules."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:62
msgid ""
"Recipes in submodules without the `[no-cd]` attribute run with the working "
"directory set to the directory containing the submodule source file."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:65
msgid ""
"`justfile()` and `justfile_directory()` always return the path to the root "
"justfile and the directory that contains it, even when called from submodule "
"recipes."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:69
msgid "Modules may be made optional by putting a `?` after the `mod` keyword:"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:75
msgid ""
"Missing source files for optional modules do not produce an error. If a "
"recipe or alias depends on a missing optional module, directly, or "
"transitively, it will be disabled. Attempting to invoke a disabled recipe or "
"alias is an error, but other non-disabled recipes can still be run."
"<sup>1.52.0</sup>"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:80
msgid ""
"Optional modules with no source file do not conflict, so you can have "
"multiple mod statements with the same name, but with different source file "
"paths, as long as at most one source file exists:"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:89
msgid ""
"Modules may be given doc comments which appear in `--list` "
"output<sup>1.30.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules.md:103
msgid ""
"Modules are still missing a lot of features, for example, the ability to "
"refer to variables in other modules. See the [module improvement tracking "
"issue](https://github.com/casey/just/issues/2252) for more information."
msgstr ""
